A||||4||JetroGT||Green Fog||||8||
Z||000000||JetroGT||01-17-2000||02:31 AM||||<BR>I got up early Sunday morining and went out to Camp Lake, cought a few gills, perch and a northern. Then when driving home the windows started to fog up. At first I thought it was just the snow melting causing the steam on the glass. So I turn up the fan speed. More fog! Same thing happened when I had my GT. When I got back home I started on it right away. Removed the washer bottle, and the jack. When I was removing the upper hose on the heater core the copper tube just pulled right out! At about that time it started to snow a bit and it was kind of getting dark. So for a quick fix I cut the copper tube so that it had a couple of flat ends it, flanged it, and clamped the two hoses together. Do these things ever go out in the summer? Thank God for my parts car! ||||reg||8
Z||000001||sdm1964||01-17-2000||06:47 AM||||Yes the go out in the summer, usally when you are away from home and have no tools!!!! I feel your pain brother. Good luck.||||reg||7
Z||000002||DJRice||01-17-2000||08:34 AM||||I just replaced mine again.  It lasted almost a year and a half.  Thank goodness for that lifetime warranty.  All it cost me was the time to fix it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||01-17-2000||02:56 PM||||Ok. Hears me under the dash this morning, unscrewing the heater core cover when the antifreeze started dripping on my face! And on my embossed fiero floor mats. Now I'm going over to my parts car to get that other core. It looks to be a newer one. How  can I get to the hoses under the spare tire compartment? Do I have to take that out too? ||||reg||1
